  "asr_text": "I'm sleepy, they say. Every morning, I see the faces of kids who come to the nurse's office first thing, and I wonder what else is behind that word. The other day, a phone screen was glowing beside the pillow of a child resting on a bed. I couldn't look away from that glow. I wanted to ask about last night, but what would happen if they thought I was a teacher who takes phones away? Would they still talk to me? If we collect all the phones in the morning and don't give them back until school lets out, can we say that's enough? I'm afraid that once we've collected the phones, we'll think everything is fine. I want that child to be able to talk about what happens at night. I don't want the nurse's office to be a place where phones are taken away. After we take a phone in, who will listen to that child?",
